---
code: cli-flag-value-not-a-number
when-fires: a numeric flag was given a non-number. cli/lib.rs parse_expect_count (--expect-files). {flag} and the {got} token.
why: 27R section 8b: --expect-files is a CI scope assertion, so a malformed count is refused rather than coerced - a silently-zero expectation would pass vacuously.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc lint --expect-files=many oracle.sh
dorc: error[cli-flag-value-not-a-number]: The `--expect-files` flag takes a
non-negative integer, not `many`.
usage: dorc [probe|plan|apply] --book=<book.sh> [--pre-source <sh>]... [--debug-argv]

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: cli-flag-value-not-a-number
{{flag}} = "--expect-files"
{{got}} = "many"
